tom: Heads up from canary testing: during an automatic rollback we observed ~300ms of 'double-serve' where both variants returned responses and the client saw inconsistent token IDs. Need a stronger handoff contract.
jess: ouch. is this from concurrent routing decisions or stale cache at proxies?
tom: mix of both. proxy marked variant B active while a few escort nodes for A hadn't drained. The simple TTL-based lease expired and the control plane removed A too early.
ravi: idea: use a signed 'commit token' with an epoch. Router flips routing only when it sees commit token X reached confidence C from escort fleet. Escort reports per-node (epoch, active_sessions).
ci-bot: ci: rollout test started for canary-v3 -> 10%
jess: how do we compute confidence? quorum? weighted health?
ravi: propose a confidence score: sum(available_capacity_percent * node_weight) / total_weight. Escort streams status every 100ms for the lease epoch. Router flips once score >= threshold or max grace timeout reached.
tom: proto sketch (very small):
```
message CommitStatus {
  string lease_id = 1;
  int64 epoch = 2; // monotonic cutover id
  repeated NodeStatus nodes = 3;
}
message NodeStatus {
  string node_id = 1;
  int32 active_sessions = 2;
  float available_capacity = 3; // 0.0 - 1.0
}
service LeaseCoordinator {
  rpc StreamStatus(LeaseRequest) returns (stream CommitStatus) {}
}
```
jess: nice. streaming reduces stalls vs synchronous ack. Router subscribes to stream and computes confidence windowed over last N samples to avoid flapping.
ops: must add force-cutover option for oncall if confidence never reaches threshold. CLI: `ri canary cutover --force <lease>`
ravi: security: commit tokens must be HMAC-signed by escort cluster so router trusts them. Also rotate signing keys with KMS.
tom: tradeoffs: lower threshold -> faster switchover but higher risk of undrained sessions; higher threshold -> slower but safer. Defaults: 70% over a 500ms window? jess: maybe 60% with 1s damping, we should run sims.
ci-bot: ci: canary progressed 10 -> 40% with no errors
jess: add observability: surface percent_confidence timeseries in Console + why_decision (list of top contributing nodes).
ops: add an emergency revert that marks epoch as ABORTED and instructs routers to stick with previous variant for Xs.
tom: next steps: ravi to prototype streaming status + HMAC token; jess to add router-side sliding window logic; ops to add force/abort CLI. I'll write a short RFC with sim results. Everyone ack?
jess: ack
ravi: ack
ops: ack
tom: thanks all :party_parrot:
